messages:
maya: FYI after recent kernel-sel swap p95 host CPU bumped ~7% for tiny streaming requests. traces point at tokenization + many small writev syscalls.

dan: confirmed on perf dashboard. writev syscall rate ~x2 for 64-256B chunks, GPUs unaffected. flamegraph: preparse::tokenize + proxy::writev hot.

lee: quick mitigation: enable micro-coalesce at proxy (buffer up to 768 bytes OR 4ms) and reuse HPACK encoder per-connection to cut alloc churn.

rita: kernel-side fix idea: include host-io penalty in kernel score so short-seq fast-path is deprioritized when writev_rate is high. patch sketch: 
```diff
- score = base_score(seq_len, mem);
- if (seq_len < 32) score -= 10;
+ score = base_score(seq_len, mem) - io_penalty(conn.writev_rate);
+ if (seq_len < 32 && conn.writev_rate < WRITEV_HIGH) score -= 10;
```

dan: i'll add a writev_rate telemetry gauge and per-shard eviction counters to correlate kvcache thrash.

perf-bot: canary posted: proxy micro-coalesce reduced writev_count by ~46%, host p95 CPU down ~5.8%, kvcache evictions down ~12% (auto).

maya: good progress. follow-ups: (1) add regression test that simulates 1000 tiny-chunk clients, (2) add kernel scoring test with synthetic high-writev signal. assigning owners and creating tickets.
